        "created_at": "2013-07-12T18:44:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dypaca\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dypaca/48/2079_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dypaca:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Well I agree, but last week&nbsp;I would have said the same thing about Chastise, Embolden, Pushing the Limits, and Solar Flare as well.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I completely understand where you're coming from, but there isn't any specification of \"Or this card has no effect\".&nbsp; It seems more like Nightmist's innate of \"Deal damage, effect happens.\"&nbsp; The damage isn't a requirement for the second half to be fulfilled.&nbsp; It just happens when you use the power or, in this case, play the card and choose that effect.</p>",
